{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting","id":944070,"title":"What's a good way for a Solar dabbler to get into RAW crafting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-04T19:06:29-07:00","id":944070,"title":"What's a good way for a Solar dabbler to get into RAW crafting?","content":"As the title says. I have a Twilight with Supernal Lore and Craft as a Caste ability, but I didn't buy any dots of Craft until very recently. Right now I have two dots of Craft (Bookmaking), but no Craft Charms other than the Excellency. If I were to pick up just one or two Craft Charms to start grinding out meaningful basic and major projects, what would you folks recommend? I already have Heaven-Turning Calculations purchased, naturally.<br /> <br /> Also, what's a good baseline investment to start making Artifacts? A hundred or so XP down the line I'd love to try to throw together a sorcerous artifact as mentioned in the sidebar by the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:09:14-07:00","id":944071,"title":"","content":"Craftsman Needs No Tools is great for a dabbler. <br /> <br /> (and for a specialist. and for everyone. it's just generally great)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:11:01-07:00","id":944072,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/igZx76o.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Also, Crack-Mending Technique means never having to say you're sorry.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the durability-enhancing Charms can come in handy <i>startlingly</i> often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-04-2016, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:29:57-07:00","id":944080,"title":"","content":"Also, buy a craft you can use all the time. Something that supports an Intimacy. &quot;Loves to cook&quot; and Craft: Cooking for example. That will get you silver points like crazy, and the Sublime Transference Charm lets you turn them into gold or white points. If you run Craft by RAW and don't get Sublime Transference, you're an idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:32:18-07:00","id":944081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944080#post944080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you run Craft by RAW and don't get Sublime Transference, you're an idiot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to personal-attack someone for having different preferences than you.<br /> <br /> (Also, while it can get rather time-intensive (depending on the methods one uses to make the books!), a person who makes books in antiquity probably does rather a lot of it; the skill is generally not picked up recreationally.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-04-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:43:20-07:00","id":944101,"title":"","content":"That was actually meant to be the &quot;general you,&quot; what's indicated in French by &quot;on.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:54:42-07:00","id":944105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944071#post944071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craftsman Needs No Tools is great for a dabbler.<br /> <br /> (and for a specialist. and for everyone. it's just generally great)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the best charm. It, a decent base pool, and a dice adder are all you really need for dabbling. Everything else is gravy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:59:56-07:00","id":944107,"title":"","content":"As for which charms to take for artifact building, there have been a number of people who've worked out strategies for that. <a href=\"https://strangercreations.wordpress.com/2015/11/25/artifactory/\" target=\"_blank\">Here is one such.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T22:17:57-07:00","id":944135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944101#post944101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was actually meant to be the &quot;general you,&quot; what's indicated in French by &quot;on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Blanket attacks against people with different preferences aren't exactly kosher either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-05-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T22:38:35-07:00","id":944139,"title":"","content":"Alucard, I'm pretty sure Lens was saying something more general. Like &quot;You'd have to be an idiot to not get this Charm&quot;. Generally speaking with a hint of hyperbole to emphasize just how important Sublime Transference is.<br /> <br /> Is there room to disagree on Sublime Transference's importance? Sure. Can that be debated? Absolutely. But in this case I'm pretty sure you'd have to reach like Stretch Armstrong to read that and take it as a personal attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:47:41-07:00","id":944195,"title":"","content":"If you want a dabbler who can do any mundane stuff and turn out the occasional artifact without bringing the game to a halt, I recommend the following six: Arete-Shifting Prana, Supreme Celestial Focus, Sublime Transference, Craftsman Needs no Tools, Flawless Handiwork Method an Bright-Forging Prana, requiring Essence 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete-Shifting Prana</b> lets you temporarily alter one of your Craft Abilities to a conceptually related one.<br /> <br /> <b>Supreme Celestial Focus</b> lets you buy additional Craft Abilities with gxp.<br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Transference</b> lets you convert one kind of crafting xp into another.<br /> <br /> <b>Craftsman Needs no Tools </b>gives you the ability to make things without tools and make basic and major projects really fast.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method </b>rerolls 10s on Craft rolls. Not spectacular on its own, but it's a prerequisite for-<br /> <br /> <b>Bright-Forging Prana </b>gives you three extra Craft Charms for one project per story.<br /> <br /> The first three Charms together give you access to virtually any Craft Ability. CNNT speeds mundane crafting immensely. Bright Forging Prana is for your occasional artifacts. I suggest the following to unlock with Bright-Forging Prana for an artifact project:<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand-Forge Hands</b> speeds the creation of an artifact immensely.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method (Repurchase) </b>rerolls 6s on Craft rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Experiential Conjuring of the True Void</b> gives non-Charm dice and a success in exchange for some craft xp.<br /> <br /> With these purchases, you can make an Artifact 3 once per story with only a week of work. With a good Intelligence rating, you should be able to make an Artifact 4 when you hit Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-05-2016, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T02:51:02-07:00","id":944206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944071#post944071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craftsman Needs No Tools is great for a dabbler.<br /> <br /> (and for a specialist. and for everyone. it's just generally great)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA bit <i>too</i> great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T05:18:10-07:00","id":944249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944195#post944195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a dabbler who can do any mundane stuff and turn out the occasional artifact without bringing the game to a halt, I recommend the following six: Arete-Shifting Prana, Supreme Celestial Focus, Sublime Transference, Craftsman Needs no Tools, Flawless Handiwork Method an Bright-Forging Prana, requiring Essence 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete-Shifting Prana</b> lets you temporarily alter one of your Craft Abilities to a conceptually related one.<br /> <br /> <b>Supreme Celestial Focus</b> lets you buy additional Craft Abilities with gxp.<br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Transference</b> lets you convert one kind of crafting xp into another.<br /> <br /> <b>Craftsman Needs no Tools </b>gives you the ability to make things without tools and make basic and major projects really fast.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method </b>rerolls 10s on Craft rolls. Not spectacular on its own, but it's a prerequisite for-<br /> <br /> <b>Bright-Forging Prana </b>gives you three extra Craft Charms for one project per story.<br /> <br /> The first three Charms together give you access to virtually any Craft Ability. CNNT speeds mundane crafting immensely. Bright Forging Prana is for your occasional artifacts. I suggest the following to unlock with Bright-Forging Prana for an artifact project:<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand-Forge Hands</b> speeds the creation of an artifact immensely.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method (Repurchase) </b>rerolls 6s on Craft rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Experiential Conjuring of the True Void</b> gives non-Charm dice and a success in exchange for some craft xp.<br /> <br /> With these purchases, you can make an Artifact 3 once per story with only a week of work. With a good Intelligence rating, you should be able to make an Artifact 4 when you hit Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> And don't forget a couple of craft-related excellencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T06:21:33-07:00","id":944267,"title":"","content":"Speaking out of experience playing an supernal Craft in an almost RAW environment I can second most of what has been already said.<br /> <br /> For Minor and Major projects Craftsman Needs no Tools is enough and let's you do crazy stuff crazy fast. It's probably everything you'll ever need if mundane crafting is all you are doing.<br /> <br /> When it comes to artifacts Crumplepunch and LadyLens described what I am successfully doing (Bright-Forging Prana is amazing).<br /> If you are playing a very specialized artisan you probably still want Supreme Celestial Focus, just to buy up the Craft (Artifacts) Dots. RAW Crafting is amazing at eating up all your regular and solar xp denpending on what you want to do and how you are playing the craft minigame.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since charms are already mentionend I will be rambling a (long) bit about my experience in the following. I'm not some clever analyst or game designer, so take it for what it is worth.<br /> .<br /> <br /> The crafting system wants you to use the crafts you have to make meaningful contributions to the game you are playing. You get crafting xp for objectives that try to capture these contributions in mechanical terms. The problem with that is that those objectives can easily be interpreted in significant different ways. The example for that already got mentionend in this thread. The projects needs to strengthen or support an intimacy you have. For my ST this at first meant &quot;playing out a crafting project in way that either makes the relevant intimacy go up one level (not possible with an already defining one) or making sure it does not go down&quot;. I was rarely able to fulfill this objective, so we talked it over and now it is &quot;Crafting things you enjoy that are supported with an intimacy&quot;.<br /> I mention this because it is important on how the crafting plays out. There was the cooking example and while I actually play a Solar Chef I don't &quot;farm&quot; crafting xp just because I make breakfast every morning. That is lame, not the system intent and you would probably better off just porting over how 2nd Edition crafting worked. At least in my opinion. I never liked the pacing-less approach of many systems out there.<br /> <br /> Well you could most certainly farm every breakfast if you read the system this way, though. But even when not, cooking is still an amazing support craft for gathering xp. And it is a good way to make people like you. That is where the crafting supports the social system and the other way around. You can get even more points if you &quot;educate&quot; your fellow player characters or NPCs to like the things you do for them and instill a few intimacies. (Having all the other players have a major intimacy on your cooking skills feels good man. And them spending willpower to prevent it from going to defining because they just happen to be there as you use Performance to awaken the appetite in other NPCs even more so!)<br /> Just be sure your ST does not think it is a good idea to seperate crafting xp for different crafts... Well it is a stretch to imagine that cooking can give you the &quot;inspiration&quot; (for which I see crafting xp as an mechanical abstraction) for a grand 10.000 years daiklave or a manse or anything even more unrelated. But well, splitting your xp pool is not the way to go about it. My ST had a big problem with it...<br /> <br /> A good support craft is something you can do with very little input and little need for specific and most importanly huge and impractical tools. You don't want every NPC to point their finger at when you magical handwave a whole feast, statue, impossible elaborate dress into existence without tools within a few seconds.<br /> Carpenter, cook, probably smith, tailor, maybe alchemist are all good professions, I think. The big ones like architect, shipwright less so. But honestly everything that you can see your character doing a lot and you as a player have fun with is good way to support crafting. Finding always new ways to aply craft within the context of a story is a fun for me. Just keep in mind that several crafts are just not that artifact friendly. Cooking for example won't bring you much options that are relevant in most games, I think. Well we are playing in the North so a few big infrastructure artifacts can be made. Tailoring and smithing are way more versatile in that sense.<br /> <br /> But back to the &quot;farming&quot; interpretation.<br /> If you do read it like this, the point-generating charms are almost worthless if you don't want to craft 10 artifacts every session. And if you don't they are amazing. And they are most certainly absolutely neccessary if you play a genius craftsman that only wants to show his skills on chosen occasions when his genius is sufficiently challenged (meaning he won't do any Minor and maybe even Major projects). Or if you have a ST with a very strict reading.<br /> Ah and make sure you know what your STs regular &quot;story&quot; is. I had a slight missunderstanding with my ST once that resulted in me not getting to reset my &quot;per Story Charms&quot; (like Bright Forging Prana) once in half a year of weekly play.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Thousand-Forge Hands is amazing for speeding up R4 and R5 Artifacts but it does not give you the infrastructure to be able to work on artifacts at all. We are playing a traveling adventure so the time and means for crafting grand things are hard to come by. Again a talk-with-your ST thing. I probably can't avoid getting &quot;Words-as-Workshop Method&quot; somewhere down the line if I want to keep all my ambitions for my character. For dabblers all the project slot charms are something to avoid though. Even if you become more than a dabbler the point generations charms do the same thing more or less (reducing crafting costs through allievating the need to buy additional project slots vs more points to buy slots with). If you don't want a follow charm of that tree (like Words-as-Workshop Method) just leave it alone.<br /> <br /> One last point and the main thing I don't like about crafting in Ex3 (which I enjoy immensely nonetheless) is how most of the craft charms are designed. Everything you need for mundane crafting is CNNT, maybe Thousand Forge Hands if you are playing an architect or a shipwright and if you are really into it Crack Mending Technique, Shattering Grasp and the durability charms (even though I still think there should be less of them that do more). And well that is about all you can do with craft in it's current state. Almost every other charm gives you only dice tricks for crafting roles which you absolutely not need for anything else than artifacts.<br /> That means if you want to realiably craft R5 and NA Artifacts you need to invest a whole lot that does not do much else for your character. You can't actually do fancy stuff with those charms. While artifacts are awesome it still takes a whole lot of time and ressources and crafting xp. I think they have paced the artifact creation for high ratings a bit too much from a character development perspective.<br /> My point with this is: As a &quot;dabbler&quot; with the charms Crumplepunch listed R4 artifacts are possible and R3 are a safe project. Everything more will take you a lot more of xp investment that may take a way a lot of otherwise more interesting ways of developing the character. My character needs to rely on buying Martial Arts Charms with solar xp to not be a liability as soon as it comes to a at least somewhat challenging fight for the combat characters in my group, i.e. everyone else. It is of course synergie problem with my group and the style we play, it is nowhere near a perfect kind of table for a main-crafter, but it works. And I think that is awesome even with the restraints the system puts crafting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow that got even longer than I expected. I apologize for boring whoever slogged through it all.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":11185,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","user":"Ryoki","date":". 08-05-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:24:45-07:00","id":944334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944195#post944195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a dabbler who can do any mundane stuff and turn out the occasional artifact without bringing the game to a halt, I recommend the following six: Arete-Shifting Prana, Supreme Celestial Focus, Sublime Transference, Craftsman Needs no Tools, Flawless Handiwork Method an Bright-Forging Prana, requiring Essence 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete-Shifting Prana</b> lets you temporarily alter one of your Craft Abilities to a conceptually related one.<br /> <br /> <b>Supreme Celestial Focus</b> lets you buy additional Craft Abilities with gxp.<br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Transference</b> lets you convert one kind of crafting xp into another.<br /> <br /> <b>Craftsman Needs no Tools </b>gives you the ability to make things without tools and make basic and major projects really fast.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method </b>rerolls 10s on Craft rolls. Not spectacular on its own, but it's a prerequisite for-<br /> <br /> <b>Bright-Forging Prana </b>gives you three extra Craft Charms for one project per story.<br /> <br /> The first three Charms together give you access to virtually any Craft Ability. CNNT speeds mundane crafting immensely. Bright Forging Prana is for your occasional artifacts. I suggest the following to unlock with Bright-Forging Prana for an artifact project:<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand-Forge Hands</b> speeds the creation of an artifact immensely.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Handiwork Method (Repurchase) </b>rerolls 6s on Craft rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Experiential Conjuring of the True Void</b> gives non-Charm dice and a success in exchange for some craft xp.<br /> <br /> With these purchases, you can make an Artifact 3 once per story with only a week of work. With a good Intelligence rating, you should be able to make an Artifact 4 when you hit Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add <b>Supreme Masterwork Focus x2 or x3</b> to that, because getting double 8s or 7s is either really nice or very necessary when dealing with artifact building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:37:18-07:00","id":944337,"title":"","content":"I will chime in to say what charms you get will be heavily influenced by what you intend to craft. If you're trying to the hit the N/A artifacts, restore lost wonders of the first age are both going to be very different from being a swordsmith or a book binder or chef.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:07:04-07:00","id":944449,"title":"","content":"My favorite is Crack-Mending just because it lets you reverse entropy. It lets you <i>reverse entropy!</i> Holy shit! What the fuck! It lets you <i>un-burn a book</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:20:27-07:00","id":944456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944449#post944449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets you <i>un-burn a book</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you have all the ash. Remember that gag in Full Metal Alchemist? The Homunculi set fire to the government records, and Ed says he's going to try and transmutate the ash back into books... Then a strong wind comes in and scatters all the ash?<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is do your book restoration in a room with a closed window, kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:57:37-07:00","id":944474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944449#post944449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is Crack-Mending just because it lets you reverse entropy. It lets you <i>reverse entropy!</i> Holy shit! What the fuck! It lets you <i>un-burn a book</i></div> </div> </div> </div>(skip ahead to about 0m 50s)<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t8WxJVBhiTY&amp;t=0m50s\" data-code=\"t8WxJVBhiTY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/t8WxJVBhiTY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:29:42-07:00","id":944519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944334#post944334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would add <b>Supreme Masterwork Focus x2 or x3</b> to that, because getting double 8s or 7s is either really nice or very necessary when dealing with artifact building.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just to confirm, are we calling 12 charm purchases dabbling here or have we moved past that? I've always seen &quot;dabbling&quot; as maybe three charms max. I mean that's 20 sessions or about 80 hours of play time at favoured rates... Or 80% of your starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:45:56-07:00","id":944532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944519#post944519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just to confirm, are we calling 12 charm purchases dabbling here or have we moved past that? I've always seen &amp;quot;dabbling&amp;quot; as maybe three charms max. I mean that's 20 sessions or about 80 hours of play time at favoured rates... Or 80% of your starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've moved past dabbling. Dabbling is Craftsman Needs No Tools and maybe a couple of other craft charms on an as needed basis, once you get a better handle on the craft system.<br /> <br /> For artifact building, you want one of the lists that people have posted here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T04:27:33-07:00","id":944783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944519#post944519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to confirm, are we calling 12 charm purchases dabbling here or have we moved past that? I've always seen &quot;dabbling&quot; as maybe three charms max. I mean that's 20 sessions or about 80 hours of play time at favoured rates... Or 80% of your starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>For dabbling, Craftsman Needs no Tools, Arete-Shifting Prana and Supreme Celestial Focus let you produce anything mundane you could want, and quickly. You need a few more if you want to produce artifacts reliably and without spending months on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:34:17-07:00","id":945600,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it further, my advice for a dabbler is to grab Craftsman Needs No Tools ASAP. This will also get you the Craft Excellency if you don't already have it and, as it requires Craft 3 as a minimum, you should have a craft dice pool of 5-6 at minimum by then too. With that, you should be able to achieve pretty much any basic difficulty in the 1-5 range without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> After that, there are around 13 to 14 other Essence 1 Solar Craft charms. My advice is to play with the Craft system a bit, get a feel for what you like and don't like about it, then buy the basic charms to eliminate the problems. <br /> <br /> You want to make something, but you never seem to have the right craft type? Arete-Shifting Prana. You want more Major Project Slots, because you're making All The Things? Tireless Workhorse Method. Not getting enough Craft XP? Brass Scales Falling. Stuff keeps breaking around you? Crack-Mending Technique. Not getting enough successes? Flawless Handiwork Method. <br /> <br /> Then buy up as many follow on charms as you need to get to where you enjoy crafting. Though, by that point, you're probably not really &quot;dabbling&quot; any more, but all of the above charms will help when making Artifacts too (if for no other reason than they're prereqs for the more artifact focused stuff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:37:36-07:00","id":945637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/944070-what-s-a-good-way-for-a-solar-dabbler-to-get-into-raw-crafting?p=944783#post944783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For dabbling, Craftsman Needs no Tools, Arete-Shifting Prana and Supreme Celestial Focus let you produce anything mundane you could want, and quickly. You need a few more if you want to produce artifacts reliably and without spending months on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And IMO, if you're making artifacts you've passed the point of dabbling in Crafting. But that's just me.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm not saying only Supernal Crafters can make artifacts, I'm just saying that if you want to make a Daiklave then you're investing more than a bit of focus into your Crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}